 "source": {
  "map": "Hillsboro CDC Figure 12.61.200-A: Downtown Plan District Boundaries (the red plan district boundary line)",
  "url": "https://api.municode.com/PublicationPdfDownload/4450",
  "page": "PDF page 703, printed CDC12.61:5",
  "sha256": "eba9a00705456447d1cc5a45f18377886ccd128c17fa0b2c304f78b8ad2818b0",
  "quote": "or/washington/hillsboro/12.61/12.61.200.txt#L2",
  "geometry": "Traced off the figure's embedded image (3742 x 2375 px) and carried onto the ground in EPSG:2913; the figure is the only statement of the boundary (the city publishes no plan-district layer: Community_Development FeatureServer holds zoning, natural resources and the comprehensive plan only, checked 2026-11-10)",
  "traced_by": "Claude (roof-rereads worker, FOLLOWUPS 181(b))",
  "traced_on": "2026-11-11",
  "drawn": true,
  "how": "The figure's embedded street-map image was registered to Metro RLIS street centrelines (snapshot as staged in data/quadfit, July 2026) by a similarity transform -- 3.19 ft per pixel, rotation -0.4 degrees -- searched over scale, rotation and offset to maximise the share of the figure's dark street lines falling on an RLIS centreline; the rotation profile peaks there and the outline then runs along the streets the figure draws it on. The red boundary line was picked by colour, closed across the gaps where street names cross it, and its inside flood-filled; the polygon keeps the full drawn width of the line, so it errs outward by about half a line width (roughly 15 ft), and a lot the line crosses is cut, not called. 515 acres.",
  "check": "Carried back onto the figure, the traced polygon sits on the drawn red line all the way round (checked at the NW corner, the north edge along the tax-lot rows, and the stepped east edge at SE 18th Avenue and SE Maple Street). Against the July 2026 Metro zoning: SCR-LD, SCR-MD and SCR-HD polygons downtown lie 0.88-1.0 inside, two large SCR-MD polygons on the south and east edge straddle it (0.39 and 0.45), and the SCR zones at Orenco, Quatama and AmberGlen lie wholly outside. The zoning runs past the 2018 figure's line in places (a lot row north of the north edge, SCC-DT blocks south of SW Oak St, SCR-HD east of the SE 18th Ave notch); the figure governs, so those lots are outside.",
  "reading": "12.61.200: 'The standards of this Subchapter apply to properties within the Downtown Plan District boundaries as shown on Figure 12.61.200-A.' 12.61.800.A.1 applies the roof standard 'in the Downtown Plan District as shown on Figure 12.61.200-A'. The figure also shades a smaller pink area, its legend 'Architectural Standards Applicability Area, Refer to Section 12.61.800'; the text binds the whole plan district, so the trace is the plan district boundary (the stricter reading; question for Steph in the roof-rereads hand-off)."
 },
